          {
            "id": 2896236,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "We'll be arriving at Branley Castle in about five minutes. But before we get there, I'll give you a little information about the castle and what our visit will include. So, in fact, there's been a castle on this site for over eleven hundred years. The first building was a fort constructed in September for defense against Danish invaders by king Alfred the Great's daughter, who ruled England at the time. In the following century, after the Normans conquered England, the land was given to a nobleman called Richard de Vere, and he built a castle there that stayed in the de Vere family for over four hundred years.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2896237,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "We'll be arriving at Branley Castle in about five minutes.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 73.16499,
                  "from": 69.085,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2896248,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "But before we get there, I'll give you a little information about the castle and what our visit will include.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 79.16499,
                  "from": 73.564995,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2896269,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "So, in fact, there's been a castle on this site for over eleven hundred years.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 85.7,
                  "from": 80.5,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2896285,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The first building was a fort constructed in September for defense against Danish invaders by king Alfred the Great's daughter, who ruled England at the time.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 97.625,
                  "from": 86.259995,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2896312,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "In the following century, after the Normans conquered England, the land was given to a nobleman called Richard de Vere, and he built a castle there that stayed in the de Vere family for over four hundred years.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 111.385,
                  "from": 98.425,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2896351,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "However, when queen Elizabeth the first announced that she was going to visit the castle in 1576, it was beginning to look a bit run down. And it was decided that rather than repair the guest rooms, they'd make a new house for her out of wood next to the main hall. She stayed there for four nights, and apparently, it was very luxurious. But, unfortunately, it was destroyed a few years later by fire. In the seventeenth century, the castle belonged to the wealthy Fennis family who enlarged it and made it more comfortable.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2896352,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "However, when queen Elizabeth the first announced that she was going to visit the castle in 1576, it was beginning to look a bit run down.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 120.799995,
                  "from": 112.56,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2896379,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "And it was decided that rather than repair the guest rooms, they'd make a new house for her out of wood next to the main hall.",
                "meta": {
